    "id": "p13-q8-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "Solve each equation for $0^\\circ\\leq\\theta<360^\\circ$.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 3,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p13-q8-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$2\\cos\\theta=1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=60^\\circ,300^\\circ$",
          "worked": "$$\\cos\\theta=\\frac12$$\nThe related angle is $60^\\circ$. Cosine is positive in quadrants I and IV.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\theta&=60^\\circ\\text{ or }360^\\circ-60^\\circ\\\\\\theta&=60^\\circ\\text{ or }300^\\circ\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 34
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-q8-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$2\\cos\\theta=-\\sqrt3$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=150^\\circ,210^\\circ$",
          "worked": "$$\\cos\\theta=-\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}$$\nThe related angle is $30^\\circ$. Cosine is negative in quadrants II and III.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\theta&=180^\\circ-30^\\circ\\text{ or }180^\\circ+30^\\circ\\\\\\theta&=150^\\circ\\text{ or }210^\\circ\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 34
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-q8-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$2\\sin\\theta+\\sqrt3=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=240^\\circ,300^\\circ$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}2\\sin\\theta&=-\\sqrt3\\\\\\sin\\theta&=-\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}\\end{align*}$$\nThe related angle is $60^\\circ$. Sine is negative in quadrants III and IV.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\theta&=180^\\circ+60^\\circ\\text{ or }360^\\circ-60^\\circ\\\\\\theta&=240^\\circ\\text{ or }300^\\circ\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 42
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-q8-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$6\\cos\\theta+3=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=120^\\circ,240^\\circ$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}6\\cos\\theta&=-3\\\\\\cos\\theta&=-\\frac12\\end{align*}$$\nThe related angle is $60^\\circ$. Cosine is negative in quadrants II and III.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\theta&=180^\\circ-60^\\circ\\text{ or }180^\\circ+60^\\circ\\\\\\theta&=120^\\circ\\text{ or }240^\\circ\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 42
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-q8-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$8\\tan\\theta=8$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=45^\\circ,225^\\circ$",
          "worked": "$$\\tan\\theta=1$$\nThe related angle is $45^\\circ$. Tangent is positive in quadrants I and III.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\theta&=45^\\circ\\text{ or }180^\\circ+45^\\circ\\\\\\theta&=45^\\circ\\text{ or }225^\\circ\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-q8-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$\\sqrt3\\tan\\theta=1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=30^\\circ,210^\\circ$",
          "worked": "$$\\tan\\theta=\\frac1{\\sqrt3}$$\nThe related angle is $30^\\circ$. Tangent is positive in quadrants I and III.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\theta&=30^\\circ\\text{ or }180^\\circ+30^\\circ\\\\\\theta&=30^\\circ\\text{ or }210^\\circ\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 34
